kind i-want-to
title I want to try a look that no terminal uses yet.
intro A look changes what a terminal shows only once a terminal uses it. vtium-config says so for a look that no terminal uses, and lets you try the look on the console first.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console
waits-for CF1 item 1: "already configured" when the look changes what the console shows

# vtium.conf already sets the font set mono for everything.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = mono
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose New look.
3. Erase the name.
4. Type big.
5. Press Enter.
6. Set Font set to mono.
7. Choose Size.
8. Choose 24 pt.
9. Set Color scheme to vga.
10. Press Esc.
at the look is made
check screen shows "No terminal uses it"
check screen lacks "already"

11. Press t to try live.
at the trial
check screen lacks "already"
12. Press Esc.

13. Press s to save.
14. Press i to install.
at the install question
check screen lacks "already"
15. Press y.
at the install
check installed look big font-size 24
check installed look big font-name mono
